{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/touring-exhibition/896","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"A Circle That Nothing Can Break","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":null,"id":"actor/2037","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Circles served as a tool for expressing emotion in O’Keeffe’s work.  In 1915, O’Keeffe began experimenting with circular forms, establishing the shape as a dominant motif in the constellation of her work. This exhibition looks at the frequency and insistence of organized circular forms in O’Keeffe’s work—from her early career to her later years—and explores their relationship with the unknown realm of emotions. Combining works of art and tangible property, this exhibition offers the opportunity to reveal the shape’s direct influence on O’Keeffe’s art and lifestyle.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Activity"}